### 5. **Sensitive Data Exposure** (OWASP A02: Cryptographic Failures)

**Issue:** Email addresses are exposed in the `/users` response. In a real app, this could leak sensitive PII.

**Recommendation:** Only return necessary fields and consider data masking:
```javascript
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  const users = getUsers(); // from database

  // Return only necessary, non-sensitive fields
  const sanitizedUsers = users.map(user => ({
    id: user.id,
    name: user.name,
    // Mask email: alice@example.com -> a***@example.com
    email: maskEmail(user.email),
  }));

  res.json(sanitizedUsers);
});

function maskEmail(email) {
  const [local, domain] = email.split('@');
  return `${local[0]}***@${domain}`;
}
```

